From a5262cbf937ea10c0b09ead7a6c904331e68cdac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 02:23:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] DolphinQt: Gen 3 team editor dialog

Desktop port of the Android build's team editor, reachable from the XD
Netplay Launcher's new "Team Editor..." button:

- Role picker (Host - GBA port 2 / Guest - GBA port 3) selecting the
  EMERALD-2/-3 save via HW::GBA::Core::GetSavePath on the configured
  Emerald ROM (falling back to the other port's ROM, matching the
  Android editor). A missing save starts from the bundled
  Sys/XDNetplay template so a fresh install can build a team
  immediately.
- Trainer/save label, party list, and a paste box that accepts either
  a raw Showdown team export or a pokepast.es link; links are fetched
  from the paste's /raw endpoint with Common::HttpRequest on a worker
  thread and marshalled back with QueueOnObject. Importing replaces
  the party (up to 6; unbuildable sets are skipped with a per-set
  reason), mirroring the Android editor's semantics.
- Remove Selected, a verified Save (re-parse the edited image, verify
  every checksum, write to .tmp, byte-identical readback, .bak backup,
  rename into place - the UICommon VerifiedWriteSaveFile discipline),
  "Show save in folder", and a message log.

All parsing/building logic lives in UICommon/XDNetplay; the dialog is
presentation and wiring only.
